X server fix 1, S5: a window-to-window CopyArea with any raster op but GXcopy
goes to miCopyArea (build-tree patch against isoriano1968/x11r6.3-amix
cb61a21, applied after zz9000hw-modes.patch and p5-1 .. p5-3).

The fast path's copyVRAMBox can only copy, so a GXxor (or any other alu)
window-to-window copy was drawn as GXcopy.  Non-GXcopy now takes
miCopyArea, whose GetSpans/SetSpans path applies the alu since S4
(p5-3-setspans-alu.patch).  GXcopy keeps the fast path from S2.

Proof: x11/bench/xorcopy, window-to-window case.

--- a/programs/Xserver/hw/amix/rtg/zz9000/zz9000draw.c
+++ b/programs/Xserver/hw/amix/rtg/zz9000/zz9000draw.c
@@ -689,8 +689,9 @@
 ** copied and, with graphics exposures on, returns the region the client
 ** must redraw (the GraphicsExpose events).
 **
-** All other cases (pixmap source or destination) fall back to miCopyArea,
-** which uses GetSpans/SetSpans (correct but slower).
+** All other cases (pixmap source or destination, or any raster op but
+** GXcopy -- copyVRAMBox can only copy) fall back to miCopyArea, which uses
+** GetSpans/SetSpans (correct but slower; SetSpans applies the alu).
 */
 RegionPtr
 ZZ9000CopyArea(pSrcDraw, pDstDraw, pGC, srcx, srcy, width, height, dstx, dsty)
@@ -713,10 +714,11 @@
     int             dx, dy;
     int             bandsUp, boxesLeft;
 
-    /* Only the window-to-window same-screen path gets the fast VRAM blit */
+    /* Only a GXcopy window-to-window same-screen copy gets the fast VRAM blit */
     if (pSrcDraw->type != DRAWABLE_WINDOW ||
         pDstDraw->type != DRAWABLE_WINDOW ||
-        pSrcDraw->pScreen != pDstDraw->pScreen)
+        pSrcDraw->pScreen != pDstDraw->pScreen ||
+        pGC->alu != GXcopy)
     {
         return miCopyArea(pSrcDraw, pDstDraw, pGC,
                           srcx, srcy, width, height, dstx, dsty);
